      "message": "With the change to nearly_flat only, the GM inverse_paths would crash during validate edges. It created a scenario where two edges intersected, but both were considered flat along the primary axis. I had originally added this check due to infinite recursion in some fuzzer bugs that would detect an intersection, add a vertex, and re-detect the same intersection effectively.\n\nNow that I think nearly_flat is actually taking magnitude into account, that workaround doesn\u0027t appear necessary and I confirmed that the two fuzzer testcases continue to pass.",
